GHDL's release build optimizes its Ada code (Makefile.in, --disable-checks:
OPT_FLAGS+=-O, ADA_FLAGS+=-gnatp -gnatn). The BCR module 6.0.0.bcr.5 passes
-gnatp but no -O, and rules_ada adds no optimization level, so its Ada is
compiled at GCC's default -O0. This adds upstream's -O -gnatn to every Ada
target.

--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -441,6 +441,8 @@
     "-fPIC",
     "-w",
     "-gnatp",
+    "-O",
+    "-gnatn",
 ]
 
 ada_library(
@@ -536,6 +538,8 @@
         "-gnat12",
         "-w",
         "-gnatp",
+        "-O",
+        "-gnatn",
     ],
     # Upstream links every simulator binary with `-shared-libgcc` so that
     # JIT-generated code and dlopen'd VPI/VHPI plugins share one unwinder with
@@ -593,6 +597,8 @@
         "-gnat12",
         "-w",
         "-gnatp",
+        "-O",
+        "-gnatn",
     ],
     # Without this the dylib/so only links thanks to lazy binding and fails
     # at dlopen time (e.g. from pyGHDL) unless the host already loaded a
